{"causes": ["The Dutch Golden Age fostered an unprecedented demand for accurate navigational tools to support global trade and colonial expansion.", "Technological advancements in copperplate engraving and printing allowed for the mass production and dissemination of detailed maps and charts.", "The need for standardized and updated maritime information across vast oceanic routes prompted governments and merchants to invest in cartographic enterprises."], "effects": ["Van Keulen's publications significantly improved the accuracy and safety of maritime navigation for Dutch and international mariners.", "His firm established a long-lasting standard for nautical cartography, influencing subsequent chartmakers for over a century.", "The widespread availability of his atlases and pilot guides facilitated further exploration and the expansion of global trade networks."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "zee-atlas", "targetName": "Zee-Atlas", "context": "Johannes van Keulen published the influential nautical atlas, the Zee-Atlas, starting in 1680, which became a standard reference for mariners."}, {"sourceSlug": "dutch-golden-age", "sourceName": "Dutch Golden Age", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "targetName": "Johannes van Keulen", "context": "The economic prosperity and maritime dominance of the Dutch Golden Age created the market and technological environment for Johannes van Keulen's cartographic success."}, {"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "amsterdam-netherlands", "targetName": "Amsterdam, Netherlands", "context": "Johannes van Keulen established and operated his prominent nautical chart publishing house in Amsterdam, the center of Dutch maritime commerce."}, {"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "nautical-cartography", "targetName": "Nautical Cartography", "context": "Johannes van Keulen's extensive publications transmitted cutting-edge nautical cartography and hydrographic knowledge across the globe for generations."}, {"sourceSlug": "willem-blaue", "sourceName": "Willem Blaeu", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "targetName": "Johannes van Keulen", "context": "Johannes van Keulen built upon the strong tradition of Dutch cartography established by predecessors like Willem Blaeu, adapting their methods to nautical specificities."}], "places": [{"name": "Amsterdam, Netherlands", "role": "Publishing Hub"}, {"name": "Dutch Republic", "role": "Operational Base"}, {"name": "Global Oceans", "role": "Area of Impact"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Johannes van Keulen", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "johannes-van-keulen"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1983825", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannes_van_Keulen"], "tags": ["Explorers & Navigators", "cultural-diffusion", "environmental-history", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Johannes van Keulen's prolific publishing house significantly advanced and standardized nautical cartography, directly enabling the Dutch Republic's global maritime trade and naval power during a critical period of expansion. His detailed atlases and pilot guides were indispensable tools for mariners worldwide, shaping ocean routes for over a century.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-11-20T18:14:17Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44790443307", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Johannes van Keulen was a 17th-century Dutch cartographer. He published the influential nautical atlas the Zee-Atlas and the pilot guide Zee-Fakkel.", "newValue": "Johannes van Keulen (died 1715) established one of the most prolific and influential nautical chart publishing houses in Amsterdam during the Dutch Golden Age, a period when the Netherlands dominated global maritime trade and exploration. His work provided essential navigational tools that facilitated Dutch commercial expansion and military prowess across oceans from the late 17th century into the 18th century. Van Keulen's meticulous cartography, often based on new hydrographic surveys and astronomical observations, critically underpinned the accuracy required for long-distance voyages.

Beginning his enterprise in 1678, Van Keulen received a patent from the States of Holland and West Friesland, granting him the exclusive right to publish sea atlases and pilot guides. His magnum opus, the *Zee-Atlas* (Sea Atlas), first issued in 1680, became a standard reference for mariners worldwide, continually updated and expanded over decades. He also published the multi-volume *Zee-Fakkel* (Sea-Torch or Sea-Beacon), a comprehensive series of pilot guides offering detailed sailing directions, coastal profiles, and harbor plans. These works were renowned for their clarity, precision, and practical utility, incorporating the latest hydrographic data and celestial observations available to Dutch navigators.

The enduring legacy of Johannes van Keulen's firm, which was carried on by his sons Gerard and Johannes II, and subsequent generations until 1885, was the standardization and widespread dissemination of accurate maritime cartography. His atlases and pilot guides became indispensable instruments for merchant captains, naval officers, and explorers, contributing significantly to the safety and efficiency of global shipping routes. The sheer volume and quality of the Van Keulen output ensured that Dutch cartographic supremacy persisted long after the peak of the Dutch Golden Age."}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-20T18:14:17Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44790443307", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Early Modern era: age of exploration, printing revolution, and religious reformation", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1654, Deventer"}, {"title": "Curiosity about unknown territories and navigation advances", "type": "Idea", "year": "1654, Deventer"}], "newValue": ["The Dutch Golden Age fostered an unprecedented demand for accurate navigational tools to support global trade and colonial expansion.", "Technological advancements in copperplate engraving and printing allowed for the mass production and dissemination of detailed maps and charts.", "The need for standardized and updated maritime information across vast oceanic routes prompted governments and merchants to invest in cartographic enterprises."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-20T18:14:17Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44790443307", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Expanded geographic knowledge and cultural exchange", "type": "Idea", "year": "1715-12-01"}, {"title": "Contributed to global exchange networks, modern state formation, and scientific revolution", "type": "Movement", "year": "1715-12-01"}], "newValue": ["Van Keulen's publications significantly improved the accuracy and safety of maritime navigation for Dutch and international mariners.", "His firm established a long-lasting standard for nautical cartography, influencing subsequent chartmakers for over a century.", "The widespread availability of his atlases and pilot guides facilitated further exploration and the expansion of global trade networks."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-11-20T18:14:17Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#44790443307", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "EXPLORES", "targetSlug": "field-290", "targetName": "Explorers & Navigators", "context": "Johannes van Keulen: Exploration voyage in explorers & navigators"}, {"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "early-modern", "targetName": "Early Modern Era", "context": "Johannes van Keulen was active during the Early Modern era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "zee-atlas", "targetName": "Zee-Atlas", "context": "Johannes van Keulen published the influential nautical atlas, the Zee-Atlas, starting in 1680, which became a standard reference for mariners."}, {"sourceSlug": "dutch-golden-age", "sourceName": "Dutch Golden Age", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "targetName": "Johannes van Keulen", "context": "The economic prosperity and maritime dominance of the Dutch Golden Age created the market and technological environment for Johannes van Keulen's cartographic success."}, {"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "amsterdam-netherlands", "targetName": "Amsterdam, Netherlands", "context": "Johannes van Keulen established and operated his prominent nautical chart publishing house in Amsterdam, the center of Dutch maritime commerce."}, {"sourceSlug": "johannes-van-keulen", "sourceName": "Johannes van Keulen", "verb": "TRANSMITS", "targetSlug": "nautica